%N A402121 Number of plane partitions of n with no repeated rows or columns, whose rows and columns are independently labeled.
%C A402121 A plane partition with r rows and c columns receives the row labels 1,...,r and, independently, the column labels 1,...,c, in all r!*c! possible ways.
%C A402121 Equivalently, a(n) counts nonnegative integer matrices with entries summing to n, with no zero or repeated rows or columns, whose rows and columns can be independently permuted to obtain a plane partition. Matrices are counted separately, without identification under row or column permutations. The empty matrix contributes a(0) = 1.
%C A402121 a(n) is congruent to 1 modulo 4.
%H A402121 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A402121/b402121.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..69</a>
%F A402121 a(n) = Sum_{P} r(P)!*c(P)!, where P ranges over the plane partitions counted by A319646(n), and r(P) and c(P) are their numbers of rows and columns, respectively.
%e A402121 For n = 3, there is one 1 X 1 matrix [3], two 1 X 2 matrices [2,1] and [1,2], their two transposes, and four 2 X 2 binary matrices with exactly one zero. Hence a(3) = 1 + 2 + 2 + 4 = 9.
%Y A402121 Cf. A319646.
%K A402121 nonn,new
%O A402121 0,4
